{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOnce the reducer, inbound, outbound and missing-version children land, `releases` syncs with Jira, but people and agents still cannot set it or ask \"what is in release X?\" from rebar: `rebar edit` has tag flags only (`src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/writes.py:155-166`), `rebar list` filters by tag but not release (`src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/reads.py:72`), and the library `edit_ticket` accepts only tag deltas (`src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py:151-186`). The epic's surfaces and docs criteria need CLI, library and MCP access, declared `outputSchema`s and the reference docs. This child adds the first local writer of `RELEASE_DELTA`, so it lands only after the outbound child, whose intent set keeps a locally set release from being stripped by the inbound set-diff.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **Edit (CLI).** Add `--add-release`, `--remove-release` and `--set-releases` (comma-separated, add-wins) to the `edit` parser in `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/writes.py`, beside the tag flags, with the same validation as tags (`src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py:207, 285-296`): `--set-releases` is exclusive with add/remove, and one name in both add and remove is an error. Generalize `_apply_tag_deltas` (`composer_edit.py:80-118`) into `_apply_list_deltas(field, event_type, ...)` and call it for tags (`TAG_DELTA`, unchanged) and releases (`RELEASE_DELTA`). Names are trimmed; empty tokens are dropped, as for tags. Update `src/rebar/_cli/help/edit.txt`.\n2. **Edit (library and MCP).** `edit_ticket` in `src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py` pops `add_releases`/`remove_releases`/`set_releases` (lists or CSV) like the tag keywords (lines 161-163) and forwards them. Add the three `Param`s to `src/rebar/_mcp_tool_specs.py` beside `add_tags` (lines 63-65) and describe them in the edit tool text (lines 347-350); the MCP tool surface is derived from the library (ADR 0119).\n3. **List filter.** Add `release_filter` to `apply_ticket_filters` in `src/rebar/reducer/_filters.py` (lines 126-165): comma-separated values, OR semantics, exact name match against `releases`, no parent inheritance (ADR 0124 decision 10). Extract the per-dimension branches into a table-driven helper first if the added branch would raise its complexity above its ceiling. Thread it as `--release` on `list` (and on `search` if `search` already exposes `--has-tag`) in `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/reads.py`, `src/rebar/_engine_support/ticket_query.py` (beside `has_tag`, line 44), `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads_cli.py` (lines 337, 544-572), `src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_view.py` (line 374), and `list_tickets(release=...)` in `src/rebar/_lib_reads.py` (beside `has_tag`, line 138), which the MCP `list_tickets` tool inherits. Update `src/rebar/_cli/help/list.txt` and `search.txt`.\n4. **Show.** `rebar show` JSON already prints all of compiled state, so `releases` appears once the reducer child lands; lean list rows keep it, because `LEAN_OMITTED_FIELDS` (`src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:379`) does not name it. Add `\"releases\": \"rl\"` to the LLM view key map in `src/rebar/reducer/llm_format.py` (beside `\"tags\": \"tg\"`, line 49) and the `rl` property to `src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state_llm.schema.json`.\n5. **Output schemas and census.** `show_ticket` advertises `ticket_state.schema.json` (`src/rebar/schemas/fetch_ticket_output.schema.json`), which gains `releases` in the reducer child; confirm `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py` passes and add a `releases` assertion to `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_schema_ticket_state.py`. Regenerate the public-API census with `python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --update` and commit `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json`; the diff must show only the new keyword parameters.\n6. **Docs.** `docs/ticket-model.md`: a \"Releases\" section (names only, add-wins deltas, no inheritance, Jira `fixVersions` sync, link to ADR 0124). `docs/event-schema.md`: name the `RELEASE_DELTA` writers (the edit composer and the inbound reconciler). Regenerate `docs/mcp-reference.md` with `python scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py`. `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`: show how to set a release from rebar.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/writes.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/reads.py`\n- `src/rebar/_cli/help/edit.txt`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/list.txt`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/search.txt`\n- `src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py`\n- `src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py`, `src/rebar/_lib_reads.py`\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_tool_specs.py`\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_filters.py`, `src/rebar/reducer/llm_format.py`\n- `src/rebar/_engine_support/ticket_query.py`, `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads_cli.py`\n- `src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_view.py`\n- `src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state_llm.schema.json`\n- `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json` (regenerated)\n- `docs/ticket-model.md`, `docs/event-schema.md`, `docs/mcp-reference.md` (generated), `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_release_surface.py` (new)\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_schema_ticket_state.py` (extend)\n\n## Testing\n\nNew `tests/interfaces/store/test_release_surface.py`, modeled on `test_tag_delta_surface.py`:\n- CLI: `rebar edit T --add-release 2.4` writes one `RELEASE_DELTA {\"added\":[\"2.4\"],\"removed\":[]}` and `rebar show T` prints `\"releases\": [\"2.4\"]`; repeating it writes nothing; `--remove-release 2.4` removes it; `--set-releases 2.5,2.6` on `[\"2.4\"]` writes added `[2.5,2.6]`, removed `[2.4]`; `--set-releases \"\"` clears; `--set-releases` with `--add-release` exits nonzero with an error; the same name in add and remove exits nonzero.\n- List: tickets A `[\"2.4\"]`, B `[\"2.5\"]`, C `[]`, and epic E `[\"2.4\"]` with a child D `[]`: `rebar list --release 2.4` returns exactly A and E (D is excluded: no inheritance); `--release 2.4,2.5` returns A, B and E; a name nobody has returns an empty list.\n- Library: `edit_ticket(T, add_releases=[\"2.4\"])` and `list_tickets(release=\"2.4\")` behave as above.\n- MCP: the edit tool with `add_releases` and `list_tickets` with `release`, through the registered server, return the same results; `show_ticket` output validates against its declared `outputSchema` with `releases` present.\n- Existing tag-surface tests pass unchanged (they pin the `_apply_list_deltas` extraction).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `rebar edit` can add, remove and set releases with the exact events and errors listed under Testing, and `rebar show` displays `releases`; pinned by the CLI tests.\n- [ ] `rebar list --release X` returns exactly the tickets whose own `releases` contain X, with no parent inheritance; pinned by the 4-ticket test.\n- [ ] Library `edit_ticket`/`list_tickets` and the MCP edit and `list_tickets` tools expose the same operations, and MCP read tools return `releases` within their declared `outputSchema`; pinned by library and MCP tests.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json` is regenerated and `tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py` passes; `python scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] `docs/event-schema.md`, `docs/ticket-model.md`, `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` and `docs/mcp-reference.md` describe the field, and the doc-drift tests pass.\n- [ ] Existing tag-surface tests pass unchanged.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` and `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exit 0, and no `src/rebar` file exceeds 800 lines.\n- [ ] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794264705143440001,"uuid":"99eddcbb-e7d3-4fe2-a51c-a29b73a72c87"}